  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "actors-note",
      "parent": "actors-access",
      "label": "<b>Access model</b>\nExternal requests enter through web ingress.\nInternal users use the governed AI gateway path.",
      "fillColor": "#ffffff",
      "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
      "fontColor": "#334155",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 380,
      "w": 180,
      "h": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "shared-note",
      "parent": "shared-controls",
      "label": "<b>Shared controls</b>\nCentral DNS, secrets, logging, and network controls support both regions without overloading the main story with subnet detail.",
      "fillColor": "#ffffff",
      "strokeColor": "#93c5fd",
      "fontColor": "#1e3a8a",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 650,
      "w": 230,
      "h": 110
    },
    {
      "id": "primary-note",
      "parent": "primary-region",
      "label": "<b>Two lanes, one gateway</b>\nChat and ingestion share policy, identity, and audit controls, while remaining operationally distinct.",
      "fillColor": "#ffffff",
      "strokeColor": "#a5b4fc",
      "fontColor": "#312e81",
      "x": 110,
      "y": 920,
      "w": 280,
      "h": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "data-note",
      "parent": "data-ai",
      "label": "<b>Private service access</b>\nWorkloads query Private DNS through DNS Private Resolver. DNS returns private endpoint addresses, and traffic stays on private paths to Azure SQL, Cosmos DB, Storage, Azure OpenAI, and Doc Intelligence.",
      "fillColor": "#ffffff",
      "strokeColor": "#fbbf24",
      "fontColor": "#92400e",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 760,
      "w": 240,
      "h": 110
    },
    {
      "id": "dr-note",
      "parent": "dr-region",
      "label": "<b>Failover semantics</b>\nAPIM shifts to regional gateway presence, runtimes redeploy warm standby, SQL uses failover patterns, Cosmos uses multi-region replication, Storage uses geo-redundancy, and AI services recover through regional standby or redeploy.",
      "fillColor": "#ffffff",
      "strokeColor": "#c4b5fd",
      "fontColor": "#5b21b6",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 500,
      "w": 240,
      "h": 100
    },
    {
      "id": "note-what",
      "parent": "leadership-notes",
      "label": "<b>What the diagram shows</b>\nUsers enter through one governed control plane. Chat and ingestion stay separate, then consume private data and AI services.",
      "fillColor": "#eff6ff",
      "strokeColor": "#93c5fd",
      "fontColor": "#1e3a8a",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 60,
      "w": 220,
      "h": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "note-governed",
      "parent": "leadership-notes",
      "label": "<b>What is governed centrally</b>\nConnectivity, firewall policy, DNS, secrets, monitoring, and logs are operated as shared enterprise controls.",
      "fillColor": "#ecfdf5",
      "strokeColor": "#86efac",
      "fontColor": "#166534",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 220,
      "w": 220,
      "h": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "note-failover",
      "parent": "leadership-notes",
      "label": "<b>How failover works</b>\nRegional ingress shifts to UAE Central. Gateway policy is synchronized, compute is warm standby, SQL follows failover patterns, Cosmos replicates cross-region, Storage uses geo-redundancy, and AI services come online through standby or redeploy.",
      "fillColor": "#faf5ff",
      "strokeColor": "#d8b4fe",
      "fontColor": "#6b21a8",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 380,
      "w": 220,
      "h": 130
    },
    {
      "id": "note-legend",
      "parent": "leadership-notes",
      "label": "<b>Legend</b>\nSolid blue = active request flow\nSolid teal = private access and shared controls\nDashed purple = failover readiness or replication",
      "fillColor": "#f8fafc",
      "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
      "fontColor": "#334155",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 560,
      "w": 220,
      "h": 110
    }
